WHY ZERO BLOCKING IS NOT A PASS

`check` reports 0 blocking and I am recording a FAIL, so I will state the
relation plainly rather than leave it to be inferred.

Zero blocking was the precondition round 3 set, and it is met. It was met at
round 4 too. It is necessary and it is not sufficient, for the reason round 3
wrote down and round 4 acted on: opus.red_evidence counts logs and reads the
`# behaviour:` header. Nine identical documents pass it. The rule is not
wrong; it is looking at the only thing a rule can look at. Signing the close
because the counter is at zero would make W-020's own rule decorative from
birth, in the opus that ships it.


